{"sounds":{"intro":"Japanese has five pure vowels and very even rhythm. Every syllable gets the same time, with no heavy stress.","rows":[["a","ah, like \"father\"","sakana"],["i","ee, short, like \"bit\"","inu"],["u","oo, short and relaxed, lips not rounded","kuruma"],["e","eh, like \"bed\"","eki"],["o","oh, like \"more\" (short)","sora"],["ou / oo","long o: hold it twice as long","arigatou"],["uu","long u: hold it twice as long","yuuki"],["r","between \"r\", \"l\" and \"d\": a quick tap of the tongue","arigatou"],["f","softer than English f, blow between both lips","fuji"],["tsu","like the end of \"cats\", then \"oo\"","tsuki"],["ch, sh, j","like English","chizu, shio, jikan"],["g","hard g, as in \"go\" (many speakers soften it in the middle of words)","gakkou"],["doubled consonant (tt, pp, kk, ss)","a tiny pause before it, like saying \"hot-tea\"","kippu"],["n","at the end of a word or before consonants: a hum \"n\"","hon, kinen"]],"notes":["Words are usually spelled in this course the way a Japanese phone keyboard writes them: \"ou\" for a long o, \"uu\" for a long u.","Desu and masu are said almost without the final u: \"des\", \"mas\".","Japanese has no stress accent like English, but each word has a pitch pattern. Do not worry about it yet."]},"numbers":[{"id":"0-to-10","title":"0 to 10","items":[["zero","zero / rei"],["one","ichi"],["two","ni"],["three","san"],["four","yon (or shi)"],["five","go"],["six","roku"],["seven","nana (or shichi)"],["eight","hachi"],["nine","kyuu (or ku)"],["ten","juu"]]},{"id":"11-to-20","title":"11 to 20","items":[["eleven","juu-ichi"],["twelve","juu-ni"],["thirteen","juu-san"],["fourteen","juu-yon"],["fifteen","juu-go"],["sixteen","juu-roku"],["seventeen","juu-nana"],["eighteen","juu-hachi"],["nineteen","juu-kyuu"],["twenty","ni-juu"]]},{"id":"tens-and-big-numbers","title":"Tens and big numbers","items":[["twenty-one","ni-juu-ichi"],["thirty","san-juu"],["forty","yon-juu"],["fifty","go-juu"],["sixty","roku-juu"],["seventy","nana-juu"],["eighty","hachi-juu"],["ninety","kyuu-juu"],["one hundred","hyaku"],["three hundred","san-byaku"],["six hundred","rop-pyaku"],["eight hundred","hap-pyaku"],["one thousand","sen"],["three thousand","san-zen"],["ten thousand","ichi-man"],["one hundred thousand","juu-man"],["one million","hyaku-man"]]},{"id":"counting-things","title":"Counting things","items":[["one thing","hitotsu"],["two things","futatsu"],["three things","mittsu"],["four things","yottsu"],["five things","itsutsu"],["six things","muttsu"],["seven things","nanatsu"],["eight things","yattsu"],["nine things","kokonotsu"],["ten things","too"],["one person","hitori"],["two people","futari"],["three people","san-nin"],["how many?","ikutsu"]]},{"id":"time","title":"Time","items":[["one o'clock","ichi-ji"],["two o'clock","ni-ji"],["three o'clock","san-ji"],["four o'clock","yo-ji"],["five o'clock","go-ji"],["seven o'clock","shichi-ji"],["nine o'clock","ku-ji"],["half past","han"],["minute","fun / pun"],["what time is it?","nan-ji desu ka"]]}],"greetings":[{"id":"hello-and-goodbye","title":"Hello and goodbye","items":[["good morning","ohayou gozaimasu"],["hello / good day","konnichiwa"],["good evening","konbanwa"],["good night","oyasumi nasai"],["goodbye","sayounara"],["see you later","ja ne"],["see you tomorrow","mata ashita"],["see you soon","mata ne"],["welcome (to a shop)","irasshaimase"]]},{"id":"meeting-people","title":"Meeting people","items":[["nice to meet you","hajimemashite"],["please treat me kindly","yoroshiku onegaishimasu"],["how are you?","ogenki desu ka"],["I am fine","genki desu"],["and you?","anata wa?"],["my name is...","watashi wa ... desu"],["what is your name?","onamae wa nan desu ka"],["where are you from?","doko kara kimashita ka"],["I am from Uzbekistan","uzubekisutan kara kimashita"],["I am a student","gakusei desu"]]},{"id":"politeness","title":"Politeness","items":[["thank you","arigatou"],["thank you very much","arigatou gozaimasu"],["you are welcome","douitashimashite"],["