Wa (written ha) marks the topic."],"rows":[["I am","watashi wa ... desu"],["is not","... ja arimasen"],["was","... deshita"],["is it...?","... desu ka"]],"ex":[["I am a student","watashi wa gakusei desu"],["this is a book","kore wa hon desu"],["he is a teacher","kare wa sensei desu"],["I am not a doctor","watashi wa isha ja arimasen"],["is she Japanese?","kanojo wa nihonjin desu ka"]]},{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Japanese often drops pronouns. Use names instead of \"you\". The word \"anata\" (you) can sound too direct."],"rows":[["I","watashi"],["you","anata"],["he","kare"],["she","kanojo"],["we","watashitachi"],["they","karera"]],"ex":[["I am Eric","watashi wa eriku desu"],["she is my friend","kanojo wa tomodachi desu"],["we are students","watashitachi wa gakusei desu"],["he is not here","kare wa koko ni imasen"],["they are teachers","karera wa sensei desu"]]},{"id":"particles","title":"Particles","text":["Small words after nouns show their job. They are the glue of Japanese."],"rows":[["wa","topic (\"as for...\")"],["ga","subject; also with suki and wakaru"],["o","object (what you do something to)"],["ni","to, at (time), in (place of being)"],["de","at / by (where or how you do it)"],["no","of, 's"],["mo","also"],["ka","question marker"]],"ex":[["I eat sushi","watashi wa sushi o tabemasu"],["I go to school","gakkou ni ikimasu"],["I go by train","densha de ikimasu"],["it is my book","watashi no hon desu"],["me too","watashi mo"]]},{"id":"verbs-polite-forms","title":"Verbs: polite forms","text":["Polite verbs end in -masu. Change it to -masen (not), -mashita (did), -masen deshita (did not)."],"rows":[["eat","tabemasu"],["do not eat","tabemasen"],["ate","tabemashita"],["did not eat","tabemasen deshita"]],"ex":[["I eat bread","pan o tabemasu"],["I do not drink coffee","koohii o nomimasen"],["I went to Tokyo","toukyou ni ikimashita"],["I did not go","ikimasen deshita"],["what did you eat?","nani o tabemashita ka"]]},{"id":"this-that-which","title":"This, that, which","text":[],"rows":[["this (near me)","kore"],["that (near you)","sore"],["that (far)","are"],["which","dore"],["this + noun","kono + noun"],["that + noun","sono + noun"]],"ex":[["what is this?","kore wa nan desu ka"],["this is a pen","kore wa pen desu"],["that book is mine","sono hon wa watashi no desu"],["which is yours?","dore ga anata no desu ka"],["that is a station","are wa eki desu"]]},{"id":"adjectives","title":"Adjectives","text":["There are two kinds. I-adjectives end in -i (takai). Na-adjectives need \"na\" before a noun (kirei na hana). To make an i-adjective negative, change -i to -kunai."],"rows":[["big","ookii"],["not big","ookikunai"],["was big","ookikatta"],["quiet (na-adjective)","shizuka (na)"]],"ex":[["it is expensive","takai desu"],["it is not expensive","takakunai desu"],["it was delicious","oishikatta desu"],["a beautiful flower","kirei na hana"],["the town is quiet","machi wa shizuka desu"]]},{"id":"wanting-and-asking","title":"Wanting and asking","text":["Add -tai to the verb stem to say \"want to\". Add -te kudasai to ask politely."],"rows":[["want to eat","tabetai desu"],["want to go","ikitai desu"],["please eat","tabete kudasai"],["please wait","matte kudasai"]],"ex":[["I want to go to Japan","nihon ni ikitai desu"],["I want to eat sushi","sushi ga tabetai desu"],["please wait here","koko de matte kudasai"],["please speak slowly","yukkuri hanashite kudasai"],["please show me","misete kudasai"]]},{"id":"existing-and-having","title":"Existing and having","text":["Imasu is for living things, arimasu for things. To say \"I have\", say \"[thing] ga arimasu\"."],"rows":[["there is (living)","imasu"],["there is (thing)","arimasu"],["there is not","arimasen / imasen"]],"ex":[["there is a cat","neko ga imasu"],["there is a bank here","koko ni ginkou ga arimasu"],["I have time","jikan ga arimasu"],["I do not have money","okane ga arimasen"],["I have a brother","otouto ga imasu"]]}],"name":"Japanese","id":"ja","badge":"Solid","note":"Polite everyday Japanese in Latin letters. Say each syllable evenly."}